content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md-77-### What is a gastric sleeve?
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md-78-- ~3 paragraphs
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md-79-- **Para 1:** Define the procedure. Explain that roughly 75–80% of the stomach is removed, leaving a narrow banana-shaped tube that holds far less food. Use plain language — no jargon.
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:80:- **Para 2:** Explain the hormonal mechanism — the removed portion produces most of the body's ghrelin (hunger hormone), so some patients may experience reduced appetite after surgery, not just smaller capacity. This is the "why it works differently from a diet" paragraph.
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md-81-- **Para 3:** Be direct about permanence — this is an irreversible change to anatomy. Then distinguish from a bypass: the sleeve does not reroute the intestines, so food still travels through the digestive system in its normal order. Frame this as context for decision-making, not a selling point.
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md-82-
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md-83-**Comparison note to weave in:** A short paragraph (or callout) comparing sleeve vs bypass — a bypass reroutes the small intestine to reduce calorie absorption; a sleeve does not reroute anything. Neither is universally better. The right choice depends on the patient's weight, health conditions, reflux history and surgeon discussion.
--
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md-85----
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md-86-
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md-87-### Eligibility
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:88:- **MBS/BMI note:** For Medicare item 31575, eligibility generally requires a BMI of 40 or higher, or a BMI of 35 or higher with a major comorbidity. BMI is only a starting point; suitability and eligibility are assessed individually by the surgeon.
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md-89-- **Bullet points to address:**
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md-90-  1. BMI is a starting point only — the surgeon assesses the whole health picture, not just a number.
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md-91-  2. The reader has tried to lose weight through diet and lifestyle changes without lasting success. Normalise this — it is expected, not a mark against them.
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md-92-  3. The reader must be prepared to commit to long-term dietary changes and ongoing follow-up. Surgery is a tool, not a one-off fix.
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:93:  4. Some health conditions may need management before surgery; suitability is assessed individually and no outcome or safety is guaranteed.
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-perth.md-94-  5. Close with a gentle nudge: the only real way to know whether they qualify is an assessment. An eligibility check is the simple place to begin.
