docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-sleeve-perth.md-102-
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:103:> Draft L283-L289: **4. How is a gastric sleeve different from a gastric bypass?** A gastric sleeve reduces stomach size but leaves the digestive pathway unchanged. A gastric bypass both reduces the stomach *and* reroutes the small intestine, which can cause some nutrient malabsorption. The bypass may produce slightly greater weight loss and tends to suit patients with significant reflux better.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-sleeve-perth.md-104-
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-sleeve-perth.md-105-> **4. How is a gastric sleeve different from a gastric bypass?** A gastric sleeve reduces stomach size without rerouting the small intestine. A gastric bypass reduces stomach size and reroutes part of the small intestine, so the procedures can have different nutritional and weight-loss effects. Reflux history, BMI, other health conditions and surgeon assessment all contribute to the choice; neither procedure is right for everyone.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-sleeve-perth.md-106-
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-sleeve-perth.md:107:> Draft L300-L305: **6. I get heartburn already. Is a sleeve still right for me?** Pre-existing reflux is an important factor to raise with your surgeon, as a sleeve can actually worsen symptoms in some patients. For those with significant GORD, a gastric bypass is often the more suitable option as it tends to improve reflux rather than aggravate it.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-sleeve-perth.md-108-
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-sleeve-perth.md-109-> **6. I get heartburn already. Is a sleeve still right for me?** Pre-existing reflux is an important factor to raise with your surgeon because a sleeve can worsen symptoms in some patients. A bypass may be discussed as an alternative for some people with significant GORD, but the choice requires individual assessment of reflux, BMI, other health conditions and surgical risk.
